## Feeling and Mind.

In itself, however, there is no true contact of the soul with the object in this sensing and representing behavior of intuition. Sensation does not experience any advancement to the rank of a psychic feeling through its partial or absolute connection with representations.

Beforehand, a spiritual value, a life-force, must be noted in the appearance; beforehand, the human being must have traveled through the territory of experience, of education. He girds himself with all his demanding self-esteem and sets out to live and act. An unquenchable urge for pleasure, for self-preservation and self-strengthening drives him, and depending on the favorable or unfavorable outcome, his condition, his mood is determined. Do these outcomes of utilitarian life, which resonate in the state of the subject, truly have a human character? Who would deny that the farmer becomes sad when there is hail damage, or happy when the weather is fruitful? And yet, as long as this one farmer thinks only himself affected, his feeling might have only a very relative difference in degree from sensation. Self-feeling, purely as such, is a dull, fruitless agitation that strives out of itself and demands a corresponding counter-feeling. Human beings rise to a true life of feeling only through their fellow human beings. It is the love of nature for the species alone that makes a perfect spiritual transposition possible for me;
